  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "2317-root",
    "title": "Inspiring Change through Curriculum Renewal by Dr. Klodiana Kolomitro Teaching and Learning Webinar Series",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "A number of entities at AKU are currently under-going curriculum review.  To support this process, the Network of Quality, Teaching and Learning (QTL_net) organized a webinar on 'Inspiring Change through Curriculum Renewal' on May 28th, 2020. ",
    "media": [],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The renewal of curriculum design is an intentional, on-going, systematic process aimed at making informed curricular decisions to provide students with learning experiences that are transformational, inspiring, and intellectually stimulating. A number of entities at AKU are currently under-going curriculum review.  To support this process, the Network of Quality, Teaching and Learning (QTL_net) organized a webinar on 'Inspiring Change through Curriculum Renewal' on May 28th, 2020. "
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The seminar was facilitated by Dr. Klodiana Kolomitro, Director of Education Development, Professional Development and Educational Scholarship in the Faculty of Health Sciences. She is cross-appointed to the Department of Biomedical and Molecular Sciences at Queen's University, Canada."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "During the session, Dr. Kolomitro discussed different strategies that influence the way we approach curriculum renewal processes including, involving our stakeholders, establishing practices and timelines, and adopting evidence-based pedagogies with high-impact practices. The presentation was followed by a Question and Answer session, in which faculty members raised important concerns regarding curriculum review processes at AKU. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "83 faculty members and staff - across 3 continents - participated in the session from the following entities:"
